  "honest_take": "The best value in this whole batch, with a maintenance asterisk. At $19.90 assembled it undercuts building your own, it does the same job as a $60 wireless BadUSB, and the design is open. But the repo is coasting: the last commit of any kind was a README edit in September 2023, and there are 35 open issues. Nothing is broken - HID injection is a stable target - but nobody is adding keyboard layouts or fixing the web GUI. Also understand the operational trade: like every wireless BadUSB, the thing that makes it convenient is an access point broadcasting from inside the target machine's USB port.",
