  "honest_take": "This is where ChipWhisperer stops being courseware and becomes a real instrument, and the price and learning curve reflect that. Two features genuinely change what is possible: the SAD trigger matches on the shape of the power trace itself, so you can trigger on a specific operation inside a target rather than on an external signal; and the internal 600-1200 MHz VCO makes clock-glitch resolution independent of how slow the target clock is. Neither of those is something you will use in your first month. Be honest with yourself about whether you need them - most people asking 'should I get into side-channel' should spend $50 on a Nano first and come back here in a year.",
