  "summary": "The same iCopy-XS hardware running a from-scratch open firmware. It keeps the screen-and-buttons cloner workflow but strips the licence tiers, tracks current Iceman Proxmark releases, and adds a plugin architecture that lets you drive the Proxmark or the Linux subsystem from JSON-described UI apps.",
  "honest_take": "This firmware is the strongest argument for owning the hardware and simultaneously the strongest argument against the vendor's pricing: it deletes the tag DRM, so the EUR375 tier and the EUR529 tier become identical devices. Know that before you order. What it does not do is change physics - you still cannot recover a DESFire AES key or clone an iCLASS SE / SEOS credential, and the ICS Decoder path it integrates is still a downgrade attack that writes PACS bits to a legacy blank and only works where the reader still accepts legacy formats. The ICS bridge has been tested only against a DIY decoder build; the commercial Nikola decoder is listed as testing pending. And the licence bars commercial use, which for a device most often bought by consultants is a real constraint.",
  "best_for": [
   "Getting the full Iceman command set with an on-device screen and battery",
   "Owners of a Basic-tier unit who want the tag types they paid a lower tier to not have",
   "Anyone who wants a Proxmark that finishes a hardnested run in their hand"
  ],
  "not_for": [
   "Commercial use - the licence forbids it",
   "DESFire or bank-card cloning, same as any other device",
   "Anyone unwilling to risk reflashing an expensive device"
  ],
