  "released": "2015",
  "price_usd": 80.0,
  "price_note": "$80 for the LAN Turtle SD, out of stock. Not on Hak5's formal discontinued list, but the successor LAN Turtle Hub ($120/$160/$200) is shipping and has taken its place in the shop navigation, so treat this as a quiet end-of-life. The LAN Turtle 3G variant IS formally discontinued.",
  "price_is_estimate": false,
  "price_checked": "2026-09-06",
  "skill_level": "intermediate",
  "skill_note": "The ncurses menu makes reverse shells easy, but you need to understand outbound filtering and where a rogue Ethernet adapter would actually go unnoticed.",
  "build_effort": "assembled",
  "build_note": "Plug into a USB port and an Ethernet cable; configure over SSH.",
  "stealth": "covert",
  "form_factor": "usb-stick",
  "summary": "A small OpenWrt computer hidden inside a case that looks like a generic USB Ethernet adapter. Plugged into a workstation's USB port and the network, it gets its power from the host, gives the host normal network access, and quietly opens an outbound shell back to you. The disguise is the product.",
  "honest_take": "This is 2015 hardware - a 400 MHz single-core MIPS AR9331 with 64 MB of RAM and 16 MB of flash - and the firmware has not been updated since October 2019. Seven years without a security update on a device whose entire purpose is to sit persistently on someone else's network is a real problem, not a nitpick. The disguise still works well, and that remains its genuine advantage over a Raspberry Pi Zero doing the same job. But it is out of stock, the 3G variant is formally discontinued, and Hak5 has shipped the LAN Turtle Hub as a replacement with USB-C, a web interface, Wi-Fi and current firmware. If you want this capability today, buy the Hub; if you want it cheap, a Pi Zero W with a USB Ethernet gadget does the same thing for about $20 and you control the software.",
  "best_for": [
   "Persistent covert remote access from inside a target LAN",
   "Blending in visually on a desk full of USB dongles",
   "Reverse SSH, OpenVPN and meterpreter callbacks",
   "Cheap secondhand lab hardware for learning implant tradecraft"
  ],
  "not_for": [
   "Anything needing current firmware or a supported security posture",
   "Buying new - it is out of stock and superseded",
   "Gigabit links (10/100 only)",
   "Environments where USB devices are locked down or whitelisted"
  ],
