   "notes": "A device deliberately disguised as an innocuous accessory, installed on someone else's machine to open a covert channel out of their network, is close to the paradigm case that computer-misuse law was written for. The disguise itself can be treated as evidence of intent. Only deploy under explicit written authorisation that names the systems, and check local law."
