  "honest_take": "For $12.50 this is remarkable value, but be clear about what is missing: no screen means no Hollywood UI and no visual confirmation, and no SD card means payloads and captures live in onboard flash only, so the covert-storage and large-PCAP tricks are off the table. The microphone is the differentiator - the hot-mic example streams room audio over Wi-Fi, which is a genuinely serious capability and one that carries much heavier legal weight than keystroke injection in most places, since recording people without consent is a separate offence in its own right. It looks like a generic USB gadget rather than a memory stick, which is slightly less covert than the T-Dongle. The embedded Marauder fork adds Wi-Fi attacks, with the standard ceiling - deauth is defeated by 802.11w/PMF, and WPA3 makes PMF mandatory.",
