  "summary": "A commercial BadUSB from Maltronics: an ATmega32u4 board that enumerates as a USB keyboard and types DuckyScript payloads. The Elite variant added a microSD slot and a DIP switch bank so you could carry several payloads and pick one physically, rather than reflashing to change the script. It is discontinued; the line continues as MalDuino 3 and MalDuino W.",
  "honest_take": "This is the entry that most needs a date check before anyone buys. The Elite is gone from the vendor's catalogue, so any tutorial or comparison recommending it is out of date. Of what replaced it, MalDuino 3 is a straight BadUSB with 128MB of onboard flash and 34 keyboard layouts at GBP35 but is currently sold out, and MalDuino W at GBP49 is the wireless one. And for context on value: a $3 CH552 board does the same keystroke injection, just without the storage, the layout coverage, the case, or a shop to email when it does not work. What you are buying from Maltronics is polish and support, not capability nobody else has.",
