  "honest_take": "This is the most conceptually vicious device in the entire catalogue, and that is the point of it: it weaponises the exact precaution a careful person takes. Someone who carries a USB condom is by definition someone thinking about USB security, and this turns that habit into the attack. Technically it is the same ESP8266 Elite implant as the Adapter, at $50 less, and it is genuinely useful as an awareness tool - it is the fastest way to make an audience understand that a trusted-looking accessory is not a trust anchor. Note the irony that Mischief Gadgets also sells the $40 Malicious Cable Detector, so the same vendor sells you both the problem and a partial answer. Practically, everything true of the O.MG Adapter is true here: 2.4 GHz only, closed firmware, kilobyte-scale storage.",
