   "notes": "Building and owning it is legal. Using it is not, against anything you do not own or lack written permission to test: keystroke injection, presenting a rogue network interface to capture a host's traffic, and copying files off are each unauthorised access or interception under the CFAA in the US, the Computer Misuse Act in the UK and equivalents elsewhere. The USB-stick disguise makes intent hard to argue about after the fact. Check your local law; this is not legal advice."
