  "stealth": "discreet",
  "form_factor": "pocket",
  "summary": "A Raspberry Pi network assessment suite that began as a Bjorn fork and has since expanded well past it: host discovery and vulnerability scanning, Wi-Fi spectrum analysis, GPS wardriving, passive monitoring, asset inventory, SIEM integration, and threat-intelligence correlation against CISA KEV, NVD CVE, AlienVault OTX and MITRE ATT&CK. It runs standalone on a handheld, meshed across several units, or as a Docker container on a server.",
  "honest_take": "First, correct the record: several forks describe Ragnar as 'the Father of Bjorn'. It is the other way round - Bjorn's repo was created in June 2024, Ragnar's in November 2025, and Ragnar's own README calls itself a fork of Bjorn. Second, note the direction of travel. Ragnar has been pulling away from the Tamagotchi-attacker genre toward network verification, monitoring and troubleshooting, which makes it more genuinely useful and much less of a toy - but it also means the heavier features want more machine than a Pi Zero 2 W has, and the project's own docs suggest 8GB+ RAM for ZAP. Treat the Pi build as the portable sensor and expect the serious analysis to happen elsewhere. Also: 2,840 commits in ten months against one open issue is fast movement with little external review, so pin a version rather than tracking main.",
