  "status": "diy-only",
  "released": "2025",
  "price_usd": 60.0,
  "price_note": "ESTIMATE, parts only, for the base build: Raspberry Pi Zero 2 WH (pre-soldered header) ~$20, Waveshare 1.44in LCD HAT with joystick ~$15 (or the 1.3in 240x240 ST7789 HAT, similar price), microSD ~$8, USB Ethernet adapter or Ethernet/USB HUB HAT ~$8-15, power bank ~$12. That is ~$60-70. The number people miss is the Wi-Fi adapter: the onboard Pi Wi-Fi cannot do monitor mode or injection here, so Wi-Fi attacks need an external USB adapter - an Alfa AWUS036ACH is ~$50, which nearly doubles the build. See the honest take about the TL-WN722N trap.",
  "price_is_estimate": true,
  "price_checked": "2026-09-06",
  "skill_level": "intermediate",
  "skill_note": "No soldering with a Zero 2 WH, but you must understand Linux networking, which USB Wi-Fi chipsets support injection, and how to recover a Pi that will not boot after an install script.",
