   "notes": "Nearly everything this device is for - ARP poisoning, DNS spoofing, credential portals, deauthentication, exfiltration - is unlawful against systems you do not own or have written permission to test, under the CFAA in the US, the Computer Misuse Act in the UK and equivalents elsewhere. Wi-Fi deauth is separately treated by the FCC as prohibited interference. The exfiltration payloads that push data to Discord or Dropbox also move third-party data onto services you do not control. Check your local law; this is not legal advice."
