  "honest_take": "It detects behaviour consistent with a cell-site simulator; it cannot prove one is present, and a quiet or well-configured catcher can go unflagged. It watches only the band and carrier the hotspot is attached to, so it is a sampling instrument, not a shield - it does not protect your phone, it tells you the airspace looked wrong. The hardware side is a used consumer hotspot, so battery health and firmware build vary and behaviour genuinely differs between units.",
