  "price_note": "Base Shark Jack $100, currently out of stock. The Shark Jack Cable edition is $120 and in stock. A newer Shark Jack Display with a screen is $120 ($220 Pro Bundle) and in stock.",
  "price_is_estimate": false,
  "price_checked": "2026-09-06",
  "skill_level": "beginner",
  "skill_note": "Flick the switch and it runs an nmap sweep. Writing your own payloads needs bash.",
  "build_effort": "assembled",
  "build_note": "Charge over USB-C, flick the switch, plug into an Ethernet jack.",
  "stealth": "discreet",
  "form_factor": "pocket",
  "summary": "A tiny battery-powered Linux computer on the end of an Ethernet plug. You walk up to a live wall jack, flick a switch, plug it in, and it runs a payload - by default a fast nmap sweep - then you pull it out and read the loot later. It is built for the fifteen seconds you have unsupervised in a corridor.",
  "honest_take": "The battery is 50 mAh. That is not a typo: it gives roughly ten to fifteen minutes of runtime on a full charge and takes about seven minutes to recharge, so this is strictly a smash-and-grab tool, not a drop box. If you want it to sit somewhere, you have to feed it USB power, at which point the Cable edition ($120, in stock, adds a CP2102 serial console) is the version you actually want. The SoC is a MediaTek MT7628DAN at 580 MHz with 64 MB of RAM and 64 MB of flash, which is fine for nmap and not much more. The base model is out of stock and Hak5 has since shipped a Display edition with a screen, so the line is clearly moving on. For the money it is a well-executed one-trick device and it does that trick well.",
  "best_for": [
   "Fast network recon through an unattended wall jack",
   "Physical-access assessments where you have seconds, not minutes",
   "Automated nmap sweeps with the results waiting for you afterwards",
   "Teaching drop-box tradecraft cheaply"
  ],
  "not_for": [
   "Leaving in place - the battery lasts about 15 minutes",
   "Wireless work of any kind",
   "Gigabit-sensitive links",
   "Anyone who needs interactive control while it is deployed (buy the Cable or Display edition)"
  ],
