  "summary": "A card-format skimmer detector that counts how many times it is read during a single insertion: more than one read means a second reader - a skimmer - is present. Functionally the same idea as Electronic Cats' Hunter Cat, sold by a European vendor with a battery in the box.",
  "honest_take": "Identical limitation to every device of this type: it detects a second magnetic read, so it catches insert and deep-insert skimmers and misses everything else - chip shimmers, keypad overlays, camera pinholes, and skimmers that read only the chip. The 'no matter how well hidden, SkimmerGuard will find it' line in the marketing is overstated; it will find a second read head, which is not the same claim.",
