   "notes": "The hardware is an ordinary consumer smart-home accessory and legal everywhere. It operates only in the 2.4 GHz licence-exempt band. As with any sniffer, the exposure is interception law rather than spectrum law - capturing other people's Bluetooth traffic can fall under wiretapping and computer-misuse statutes in the US, UK and EU even when the traffic is unencrypted. Sniff only what you own or are authorised in writing to test."
