  "stealth": "covert",
  "form_factor": "usb-stick",
  "summary": "A device that harvests power from a USB port, multiplies the voltage and dumps it back into the data lines, destroying unprotected hardware. The V4 adds an internal battery so it works on powered-off devices, plus BLE remote, timer and magnet triggers, and adapters for Lightning, USB-C, Ethernet, HDMI and DisplayPort.",
  "honest_take": "Be clear what this is: it is not a pentest tool, it is a destruction tool. It reads nothing, proves nothing about software security, and the only legitimate use is deliberately stress-testing port protection on hardware you own or manufacture. The covert triggers (magnet, timer, BLE) exist because customers want to destroy things without being seen doing it, and in most jurisdictions using one on someone else's equipment is criminal damage with an unusually clear evidence trail. Also note it can wreck the port, the motherboard, or an entire industrial system in one press.",
